Testing was carried out at several levels to make sure the system is correct, safe, and easy to use. Unit tests verified individual functions such as form validation, template loading, and file export, while integration tests confirmed that the frontend, backend, and AI service work together correctly. System testing covered complete user journeys from login to download. Because the output comes from an AI model, a separate quality check was performed on generated documents. Reviewers confirmed that all required clauses were present, that names, dates, and amounts matched the inputs, that no clauses contradicted one another, and that the disclaimer appeared. Test cases included valid and invalid logins, document generation with complete and incomplete inputs, editing and saving versions, exporting to PDF, and entering malicious text to confirm that inputs are sanitized. Usability testing was done by asking a small group of people who were not developers to complete a task, then recording how long it took and how they rated the experience. Security testing checked authentication, data protection, and input handling, and performance testing measured the average generation time. The results, including the number of tests run, the pass rate, and the bugs found and fixed, are recorded in the test report.
